      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOVEREIGN CRUST (3) has the clearest upward profile, coming off a determined Mdn win at this track when she beat Peanut Butter by a neck and backed up her soft-track second to Pancho's Place. Turned in a strong rating last start and she can build on that with the confidence now under her belt. WHATYOUTALKINBOUT (2) is the main danger, with two wins at this track, a strong record for Lucy Fiore and enough excuse from last start when steadied and bumped late after finishing third the run before. OFFSHORE (5) brings proven 1100m form and was only beaten just under two lengths at long odds behind Wiluna Lass, although she has to turn that close run into a more decisive finishing effort. VIRESHA (6) is harder to trust on this season's form, but her latest sixth was within three lengths after being tightened and she has enough distance background to press for a minor result if she sharpens late. HOLD MY WINE (1) can bounce back.",
